goal: list of the most common charts used in business
====================================
Here are the most common charts used in business, what they’re good for, and when people usually reach for them 👇

$$$ 0. Bar / Column Chart: 

Best for: Comparing values across categories
Typical uses: Sales by product, revenue by region, expenses by department
👉 Easy to read, exec-friendly, probably the most used chart in business.

links = (0a. https://github.com/AkinwaleOwi/charts_python/blob/main/bar_graph_each_bar_a_different_color_3d, 0b. https://github.com/AkinwaleOwi/charts_python/blob/main/bar_graph_each_bar_a_different_color_3d)


$$$. 1. Line Chart

Best for: Trends over time
Typical uses: Monthly sales, stock prices, website traffic, KPIs over time
👉 Perfect when time is involved and you want to show growth, decline, or seasonality.

links = 1a.https://github.com/AkinwaleOwi/charts_python/blob/main/python_line_chart_with_each_line_a_different_color_3D , 1b. https://github.com/AkinwaleOwi/charts_python/blob/main/line_chart_each_line_a_different_color_2d , 1c. https://github.com/AkinwaleOwi/charts_python/blob/main/line_graph_dotted_line_width_work , 1d. https://github.com/AkinwaleOwi/charts_python/blob/main/line_graph_multiple_lines_dotted , 1e. https://github.com/AkinwaleOwi/charts_python/blob/main/line_graph_solid_line_hex_color, 1f. https://github.com/AkinwaleOwi/charts_python/blob/main/line_graph_dotted_line , 1g. https://github.com/AkinwaleOwi/charts_python/blob/main/line_graph_solid_line

$$$. 2. Pie Chart

Best for: Showing parts of a whole
Typical uses: Market share, budget allocation
👉 Works only when there are few categories. Overused and often misused 😅

links = 2a. https://github.com/AkinwaleOwi/charts_python/blob/main/pie_chart_chatgpt_3d , 2b. https://github.com/AkinwaleOwi/charts_python/blob/main/pie_chart2d_ChatGpt

3. Stacked Bar / Stacked Column

Best for: Comparing totals and composition
Typical uses: Revenue by region split by product line
👉 Good for storytelling, but can get messy if there are many segments.

4. Area Chart

Best for: Trends + magnitude over time
Typical uses: Cumulative sales, user growth
👉 Like a line chart, but with more visual “weight.”

$$$. 5. Scatter Plot

Best for: Relationships between variables
Typical uses: Price vs. demand, ad spend vs. conversions
👉 Great for analysis and spotting correlations (and outliers).

Links = 5a. https://github.com/AkinwaleOwi/charts_python/blob/main/scatterplot_two_different_line_colors_2D

$$$. 6. Histogram

Best for: Distribution of data
Typical uses: Customer age distribution, delivery times
👉 Popular with analysts, less so in exec decks.

Links = 6a. https://github.com/AkinwaleOwi/charts_python/blob/main/histogram_2d , 6b. https://github.com/AkinwaleOwi/charts_python/blob/main/histogram_3d


7. Waterfall Chart

Best for: Showing how a starting value changes step by step
Typical uses: Profit breakdown, cash flow analysis
👉 A finance team favorite.

8. Table (yes, really)

Best for: Exact values
Typical uses: Financial statements, detailed reports
👉 Not flashy, but often necessary.

9. Dashboard Combo (mixed charts)

Best for: Monitoring performance
Typical uses: Executive dashboards, KPI tracking
👉 Usually a mix of bar, line, and KPI tiles.

